1
00:00:08,500 --> 00:00:11,817
The world, what a glorious place.

2
00:00:11,900 --> 00:00:16,097
Seek freedom, and it will lie
stretched out before your eyes.

3
00:00:16,180 --> 00:00:22,540
If the endless dream guides your restless
spirit, seize it, raise your flag,

4
00:00:22,820 --> 00:00:23,960
and stand tall.

5
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:32,677
I think back to the time
when my search first began.

6
00:00:32,760 --> 00:00:35,337
I left behind those shores of sand.

7
00:00:35,420 --> 00:00:38,620
For the endless everlasting
world out there.

8
00:00:39,540 --> 00:00:42,817
I know that with this
burning passion I leave me.

9
00:00:42,900 --> 00:00:48,580
Someday, somewhere, I'll finally see the
light I have searched for everywhere?.

10
00:00:53,140 --> 00:00:55,737
When the summer sun is shining.

11
00:00:55,820 --> 00:00:58,717
Shaking the sails of my heart. But I know.

12
00:00:58,800 --> 00:01:04,437
A brand new world

13
00:01:04,520 --> 00:01:05,817
that has been hiding.

14
00:01:05,900 --> 00:01:08,837
Has opened up its doors for me to go.

15
00:01:08,920 --> 00:01:11,880
A great, long blue sky.

16
00:01:12,900 --> 00:01:15,357
Wearing in the tumble waves.

17
00:01:15,440 --> 00:01:17,857
From all despair I can be saved.

18
00:01:17,940 --> 00:01:21,177
For the horizon on the other side is.

19
00:01:25,680 --> 00:01:28,557
And though I travel far
from where my search began.

20
00:01:28,640 --> 00:01:31,177
Over streets of green and shores of sand.

21
00:01:31,260 --> 00:01:34,640
Through the endless
everlasting world out there.

22
00:01:35,380 --> 00:01:38,697
I know that with this
burning passion driving me.

23
00:01:38,780 --> 00:01:44,420
Someday somewhere I'll finally see the
light I will search for everywhere?

24
00:01:56,320 --> 00:01:57,150
Yahoo!

25
00:01:57,233 --> 00:01:58,680
Good God! Thank you!

26
00:01:59,320 --> 00:02:01,957
I can't believe after all the
suffering we've endured to

27
00:02:02,040 --> 00:02:05,217
find Sky Island that it turned
out to be the city of gold!

28
00:02:05,300 --> 00:02:08,897
Which must be your way to reward
me for my good behavior, right God?

29
00:02:08,980 --> 00:02:10,700
You're just great!

30
00:02:11,300 --> 00:02:12,130
Shut up.

31
00:02:12,240 --> 00:02:15,677
Ten minutes ago, you were scared this
god was gonna kill you, remember?

32
00:02:15,760 --> 00:02:17,140
Well, call me shallow,

33
00:02:17,340 --> 00:02:21,537
but I don't care how scared I get as
long as somebody has gold waiting for me.

34
00:02:21,620 --> 00:02:24,700
So do you fear or praise
this god? I'm confused.

35
00:02:25,220 --> 00:02:28,338
All right, I'm done keeping
up with your mood swings.

36
00:02:47,940 --> 00:02:49,260
Ha-ha-ha. Useless.

37
00:02:58,760 --> 00:03:00,240
What is this?

38
00:03:00,680 --> 00:03:04,477
My money says that this is where we're
supposed to find the next ordeal,

39
00:03:04,560 --> 00:03:06,957
which means another priest,
so you two stay awake.

40
00:03:07,040 --> 00:03:07,870
Oh, no.

41
00:03:08,180 --> 00:03:11,356
I think one ordeal is enough
of a nightmare for today.

42
00:03:11,560 --> 00:03:13,457
Which one seems like it could be out here?

43
00:03:13,540 --> 00:03:15,060
String? Iron? Swamp?

44
00:03:15,160 --> 00:03:16,840
I'm so nervous. Relax.

45
00:03:17,120 --> 00:03:18,417
It's just a grassy field.

46
00:03:18,500 --> 00:03:19,330
Open your eyes.

47
00:03:19,413 --> 00:03:20,337
It's not just a field.

48
00:03:20,420 --> 00:03:24,037
It's a field with a thousand impelled
skulls set out like trophies to scare us,

49
00:03:24,120 --> 00:03:26,180
and it's working! You're right.

50
00:03:26,340 --> 00:03:27,634
I wonder who did this.

51
00:03:30,400 --> 00:03:31,753
Hey, what's that smoke?

52
00:03:34,920 --> 00:03:35,800
We're dead!

53
00:03:59,180 --> 00:04:01,860
What's wrong with that guy? Paramecia.

54
00:04:02,280 --> 00:04:06,320
Wiper, we fighting? Not
now. Keep moving. You.

55
00:04:07,520 --> 00:04:08,440
We're ready!

56
00:04:08,680 --> 00:04:09,620
Come on down!

57
00:04:09,800 --> 00:04:10,800
We'll cream you!

58
00:04:11,280 --> 00:04:13,220
Make your move, big guys!

59
00:04:15,480 --> 00:04:18,220
You sound and stink like Blue Sea people,

60
00:04:18,460 --> 00:04:22,048
which means you're the ones
causing all the chaos in Skypiea!

61
00:04:22,600 --> 00:04:26,200
Luffy, that's the gorilla we
saw back on the White Sea. Look!

62
00:04:26,680 --> 00:04:28,160
What got into him?

63
00:04:29,120 --> 00:04:31,414
There's a guy running around out there.

64
00:04:32,300 --> 00:04:34,080
Hey, stop! What do you want?

65
00:04:34,220 --> 00:04:35,300
To destroy you!

66
00:04:37,040 --> 00:04:39,240
Just blow us up and get it over with!

67
00:04:40,440 --> 00:04:44,440
If you don't want to die, then go
back to your blue sea immediately.

68
00:04:44,700 --> 00:04:48,171
Because I promise if you do
anything stupid on this island,

69
00:04:49,660 --> 00:04:51,440
we'll execute you with Enaru.

70
00:04:53,580 --> 00:04:56,077
They're up here trying
to kill this guy, Enaru?

71
00:04:56,160 --> 00:04:59,500
Then that means that these
gorillas are different.

72
00:05:00,040 --> 00:05:03,197
If different means they're not priests,
then that means they don't have to kill us.

73
00:05:03,280 --> 00:05:07,497
So for the sake of keeping all of our body
parts attached, can we please sail on?

74
00:05:07,580 --> 00:05:08,420
Not a chance!

75
00:05:08,620 --> 00:05:09,917
What do you say to a fair fight?

76
00:05:10,000 --> 00:05:11,120
Just you and me!

77
00:05:12,080 --> 00:05:14,060
I'm begging you! Please stop!

78
00:05:14,820 --> 00:05:16,737
You stay on that tree ranch!

79
00:05:16,820 --> 00:05:18,620
I'm coming to you! Usam!

80
00:05:20,340 --> 00:05:21,260
Hands off!

81
00:05:21,700 --> 00:05:22,759
Try to fight here!

82
00:05:23,080 --> 00:05:24,780
Uphold our honor! I have to!

83
00:05:25,400 --> 00:05:26,720
On second thought,

84
00:05:26,940 --> 00:05:30,457
you'll probably end up
killing each other before

85
00:05:30,540 --> 00:05:33,481
you even have a chance to
make it off this island.

86
00:05:37,500 --> 00:05:39,417
I wonder why they're up here.

87
00:05:39,500 --> 00:05:40,997
I'm not sure.

88
00:05:41,080 --> 00:05:42,717
Must be pretty serious.

89
00:05:42,800 --> 00:05:46,077
But they seem to be enemies
of Enteru as well as us.

90
00:05:46,160 --> 00:05:47,157
You know.

91
00:05:47,240 --> 00:05:50,217
I really do hate this place.

92
00:05:50,300 --> 00:05:51,420
Let's keep moving.

93
00:06:06,720 --> 00:06:07,840
I'll cover you!

94
00:06:09,080 --> 00:06:11,021
Get it out of that thing's mouth!

95
00:06:13,060 --> 00:06:14,160
Move in now!

96
00:06:55,740 --> 00:06:58,120
We've been sailing forever, Sanji.

97
00:06:58,220 --> 00:06:59,220
When can we stop?

98
00:07:01,020 --> 00:07:02,697
Can we stop now? Soon.

99
00:07:02,780 --> 00:07:04,060
The sun's going down.

100
00:07:04,260 --> 00:07:06,613
I wonder what we'll run into after dark.

101
00:07:06,860 --> 00:07:09,897
Do you think we can make it
to the altar before then?

102
00:07:09,980 --> 00:07:11,300
No, I don't.

103
00:07:12,760 --> 00:07:15,517
I can barely see the sunset
through those clouds.

104
00:07:15,600 --> 00:07:18,247
I'm surprised they even
have sunsets up here.

105
00:07:31,360 --> 00:07:33,500
We can handle these guys.

106
00:07:35,940 --> 00:07:38,140
Yeah, help the others! Got it.

107
00:07:54,220 --> 00:07:55,050
Chopper!

108
00:07:55,133 --> 00:07:56,220
Where are you, Chopper?

109
00:07:57,220 --> 00:07:59,040
If you can hear me, answer!

110
00:07:59,500 --> 00:08:00,540
Are you there?

111
00:08:01,340 --> 00:08:04,277
Look, her mast is gone and
a wing is ripped in half.

112
00:08:04,360 --> 00:08:06,297
What's he done to her since we left?

113
00:08:06,380 --> 00:08:08,317
Obviously, the Going Merry was attacked.

114
00:08:08,400 --> 00:08:10,297
Chopper couldn't have done that to her.

115
00:08:10,380 --> 00:08:11,210
Chopper!

116
00:08:11,293 --> 00:08:12,920
I'm sorry we took so long!

117
00:08:13,240 --> 00:08:14,337
You can come out now!

118
00:08:14,420 --> 00:08:16,580
You'll be safe! I promise! Yes!

119
00:08:17,080 --> 00:08:19,727
At least give us a sign
that you're not dead!

120
00:08:21,500 --> 00:08:23,680
So I guess that means that he's dead.

121
00:08:24,100 --> 00:08:26,218
Would it kill you to think positive?

122
00:08:26,640 --> 00:08:28,820
Hey, Chipper! Come out!

123
00:08:29,040 --> 00:08:31,760
Because Nomi's scared, and I'm tired!

124
00:08:34,540 --> 00:08:35,370
Hi.

125
00:08:40,320 --> 00:08:43,300
Everything stayed ship-shape
while you were gone.

126
00:08:44,920 --> 00:08:47,820
You don't have to lie to
us, Chopper. Be strong.

127
00:08:47,980 --> 00:08:49,921
Tell us everything that happened.

128
00:08:55,800 --> 00:08:57,920
Please help me as I put a corkscrew.

129
00:09:05,200 --> 00:09:06,600
We're soaking wet.

130
00:09:08,320 --> 00:09:09,420
Check it out.

131
00:09:09,700 --> 00:09:10,697
We found it.

132
00:09:10,780 --> 00:09:14,157
There's the altar with the
Going Mary sitting right on top!

133
00:09:14,240 --> 00:09:15,070
Huh?

134
00:09:15,840 --> 00:09:16,670
Yes!

135
00:09:17,520 --> 00:09:18,560
Mommy! Robin!

136
00:09:19,260 --> 00:09:20,960
I missed you so much!

137
00:09:21,580 --> 00:09:25,277
Sorry to keep you waiting, but I
beat the ordeal of love to get here!

138
00:09:25,360 --> 00:09:27,500
I thought it was fierce, not love.

139
00:09:27,860 --> 00:09:30,457
If that was love, I don't
ever want to find it again!

140
00:09:30,540 --> 00:09:31,599
Anyway, who cares?

141
00:09:31,700 --> 00:09:32,530
We're alive!

142
00:09:32,900 --> 00:09:33,730
Woohoo!

143
00:09:33,813 --> 00:09:35,816
Sounds like they're happy to be here.

144
00:09:36,280 --> 00:09:37,240
Safe and sound.

145
00:09:45,480 --> 00:09:47,100
Where's the… mast?

146
00:09:47,540 --> 00:09:48,460
Uh, look.

147
00:09:48,760 --> 00:09:52,240
I tried, but it didn't
matter how hard I fought.

148
00:09:52,360 --> 00:09:54,301
He still kept burning everything.

149
00:09:54,400 --> 00:09:57,000
I promise I did everything I could. Yeah?

150
00:09:57,280 --> 00:09:59,574
Well, are you going to be okay or what?

151
00:10:03,700 --> 00:10:06,517
You must have been scared
facing that guy by yourself.

152
00:10:06,600 --> 00:10:10,365
It's a good thing he set the mast
on fire instead of you, right?

153
00:10:10,780 --> 00:10:13,604
We can figure out the
details on the ship later.

154
00:10:15,860 --> 00:10:19,560
I promise to become a more
dependable man starting right now!

155
00:10:19,900 --> 00:10:22,537
Chopper, stop yelling at the
altar and tell me something.

156
00:10:22,620 --> 00:10:24,561
How'd you get rid of that priest?

157
00:10:24,880 --> 00:10:28,717
I used the whistle the Sky Knight gave
us, and he showed up to rescue me.

158
00:10:28,800 --> 00:10:29,880
Oh, where is he?

159
00:10:30,040 --> 00:10:31,220
I don't see him.

160
00:10:41,980 --> 00:10:44,660
He's willing to sacrifice
this much for us,

161
00:10:44,860 --> 00:10:47,507
even though he gave us
that whistle for free.

162
00:10:48,260 --> 00:10:49,797
If it wasn't for the sky night,

163
00:10:49,880 --> 00:10:53,097
you guys probably wouldn't have
a ship, and I'd for sure be dead.

164
00:10:53,180 --> 00:10:57,592
I got a bunch of questions for him,
but I guess I'll wait till he wakes up.

165
00:10:57,680 --> 00:10:59,440
We owe you a thanks as well.

166
00:11:00,200 --> 00:11:01,030
Beee!

167
00:11:04,220 --> 00:11:05,050
Luffy!

168
00:11:07,200 --> 00:11:10,057
The Going Mary's trashed,
and it'll be dark soon,

169
00:11:10,140 --> 00:11:14,316
so there's no chance we'll make it
back to Angel Island until tomorrow.

170
00:11:14,600 --> 00:11:17,857
We should hop over to land and
make camp on shore for the night.

171
00:11:17,940 --> 00:11:18,980
Huh? Why there?

172
00:11:19,260 --> 00:11:21,457
Because if we stay here
and someone attacks us,

173
00:11:21,540 --> 00:11:23,497
the first thing to take a
beating will be our ship.

174
00:11:23,580 --> 00:11:25,404
Would you use your head, Luffy?

175
00:11:25,700 --> 00:11:26,530
Not to mention,

176
00:11:26,613 --> 00:11:29,777
it's easier to fight from land than
from an altar floating on a cloud.

177
00:11:34,160 --> 00:11:36,920
This isn't a party,
we're in enemy territory.

178
00:11:37,340 --> 00:11:38,300
Now calm down!

179
00:11:47,180 --> 00:11:48,160
Excellent work!

180
00:11:48,980 --> 00:11:52,077
Now, based on your reports,
we've learned that...

181
00:11:52,160 --> 00:11:56,097
The priests can predict our movements
using a power they like to call Mantara,

182
00:11:56,180 --> 00:11:58,357
and the bird blows flames
and the spear burns you?

183
00:11:58,440 --> 00:12:00,852
But most importantly, we've learned this!

184
00:12:00,980 --> 00:12:04,457
The City of Gold is not a thousand
leagues under the sea as we had thought,

185
00:12:04,540 --> 00:12:07,860
but it is hidden somewhere
on this very island! No way!

186
00:12:08,520 --> 00:12:10,638
That was the first thing I told you!

187
00:12:10,960 --> 00:12:13,600
So, what is this mantra
business all about?

188
00:12:13,920 --> 00:12:17,097
Maybe it's some kind of sixth
sense you only get up here.

189
00:12:17,180 --> 00:12:18,010
Sixth sense?

190
00:12:18,540 --> 00:12:21,481
Yo, Chopper, do I need to
grind this down anymore?

191
00:12:21,580 --> 00:12:23,580
Yes, it needs to be a fine powder.

192
00:12:23,820 --> 00:12:26,879
He suffered a lot of damage
to his digestive system.

193
00:12:31,200 --> 00:12:35,537
This is it an adventure
with gold at the end I can't

194
00:12:35,620 --> 00:12:40,637
wait glad to see someone on
my side I'm ready Luffy no

195
00:12:40,720 --> 00:12:43,137
did you forget what the
scary gorilla guy said about

196
00:12:43,220 --> 00:12:46,577
execution god will be really

197
00:12:46,660 --> 00:12:51,517
mad sounds like fun well we

198
00:12:51,600 --> 00:12:53,737
wouldn't be very good pirates
if we turned our backs

199
00:12:53,820 --> 00:12:58,137
on gold so let's not it won't
be easy you know everybody

200
00:12:58,220 --> 00:13:03,017
up here already hates us
which means I'm in come on

201
00:13:03,100 --> 00:13:07,757
aren't you even a little
frightened of the wrath of God?

202
00:13:07,840 --> 00:13:10,400
I mean, I want to live, don't you?

203
00:13:19,840 --> 00:13:23,140
Gold, and it's all waiting for us!

204
00:13:25,800 --> 00:13:27,271
Kamakiri, you gotta move!

205
00:13:28,980 --> 00:13:31,509
Thanks, I owe you one
after that, Kamakiri.

206
00:13:34,940 --> 00:13:35,770
Kamakiri!

207
00:13:41,920 --> 00:13:42,750
Wiper!

208
00:13:42,920 --> 00:13:44,740
Kamikitty's taking a hit! Huh?

209
00:13:45,020 --> 00:13:45,960
What happened?

210
00:13:51,240 --> 00:13:52,070
Damn.

211
00:13:52,153 --> 00:13:53,760
So close to victory.

212
00:13:54,620 --> 00:13:57,380
But you never even had a chance.

213
00:13:57,860 --> 00:14:01,380
When night falls, we'll have
an even greater advantage.

214
00:14:10,360 --> 00:14:11,680
We're moving out!

215
00:14:11,900 --> 00:14:14,537
Grab all our wounded and meet
back at the rendezvous point!

216
00:14:14,620 --> 00:14:15,450
Now!

217
00:14:18,160 --> 00:14:19,880
You're not getting away!

218
00:14:20,840 --> 00:14:21,670
Om, wait!

219
00:14:23,060 --> 00:14:24,300
What is it?

220
00:14:25,280 --> 00:14:27,680
We have been summoned by God Inaru.

221
00:14:41,900 --> 00:14:42,730
Hmm.

222
00:14:43,460 --> 00:14:44,740
Ah! Boring!

223
00:14:45,380 --> 00:14:47,909
Nobody told you to
watch the boiling water.

224
00:14:48,120 --> 00:14:50,420
You have one job and one job only.

225
00:14:50,540 --> 00:14:53,317
Take the distilled water
and fill up the canteens.

226
00:14:53,400 --> 00:14:55,257
So, make sure that happens.

227
00:14:55,340 --> 00:14:57,752
We'll need fresh drinking water tomorrow.

228
00:14:58,960 --> 00:15:00,240
Hmph. Whatever.

229
00:15:01,420 --> 00:15:03,497
Sanji, we found tons of great stuff!

230
00:15:03,580 --> 00:15:04,410
Excellent.

231
00:15:04,493 --> 00:15:05,323
Let's see the hall.

232
00:15:05,740 --> 00:15:08,617
We found walnuts, aloe, bananas, garlic...

233
00:15:08,700 --> 00:15:09,837
Rats and frogs, too.

234
00:15:09,920 --> 00:15:11,626
Nice, it all goes in the pot.

235
00:15:12,360 --> 00:15:13,190
Disgusting!

236
00:15:13,273 --> 00:15:15,117
You don't expect us to
eat that mess, do you?

237
00:15:15,200 --> 00:15:16,380
Oh, silly me.

238
00:15:16,740 --> 00:15:19,480
Nami, I promise, I'll take the garlic out.

239
00:15:19,720 --> 00:15:21,661
The garlic's the only good thing!

240
00:15:21,760 --> 00:15:24,172
Is our navigator having another meltdown?

241
00:15:25,400 --> 00:15:28,620
Now that's what I call a gem. It's huge!

242
00:15:29,200 --> 00:15:31,440
Big, yes, but it's not a gemstone.

243
00:15:32,240 --> 00:15:34,177
Hey, that's a big salt crystal.

244
00:15:34,260 --> 00:15:36,300
Nice find, Robin, dear.

245
00:15:36,800 --> 00:15:38,212
I found it on the shore.

246
00:15:38,480 --> 00:15:40,833
And I figured we'd find some use for it.

247
00:15:41,000 --> 00:15:45,588
Not only is salt vital to survival, but
without it, my food would taste awful.

248
00:15:46,740 --> 00:15:49,200
If I take half of the garlic and olive,

249
00:15:49,460 --> 00:15:51,837
then I can make antiseptic
and burn ointment?

250
00:15:51,920 --> 00:15:53,880
and use it to heal the Second.

251
00:15:54,780 --> 00:15:55,610
Yeah?

252
00:15:55,693 --> 00:15:56,523
Need any frog?

253
00:15:56,606 --> 00:15:57,436
No, no frog.

254
00:15:57,519 --> 00:15:58,617
Zoro, you're not doing anything.

255
00:15:58,700 --> 00:16:00,320
I got a little job for you.

256
00:16:03,540 --> 00:16:07,980
Oh, Sanji, my swords were not
meant to be used like this.

257
00:16:08,220 --> 00:16:12,514
Yeah, but disobey the chef and you
